{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-run-phone-tracker-engine-a-01","date":"2026-11-24","lens":"6","surface":"phone","area":"phone/tracker-engine","refs":["F-phone-900"],"severity":"S3","title":"On a stalled line the exercise demo shows an empty box for good, and the how-to drawings never appear","what":"The first time a member opens an exercise that has a demo clip, the phone downloads it with no time limit. Android's networking never gives up by itself, so on a weak gym signal that stalls the download waits for ever: the frame stays an empty grey box, the how-to sheet never falls back to its drawings, and every later visit to that exercise waits on the same stuck download until the app is closed.","expected":"A download that takes too long is given up after a set time, logged, and the screen shows the drawings instead; the next visit tries again.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/tracker/clips/clipFs.ts:19-22","apps/mobile/src/tracker/clips/clipCache.ts:88-119","apps/mobile/src/tracker/components/ExerciseClip.tsx:87-103","apps/mobile/src/lib/fetchTimeout.ts:2-12"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"clip-download-has-no-time-limit","who":"members","how_often":"on a weak or stalled connection, first visit to an exercise with a clip","fix_line":"Give the clip download a time limit, treat a timeout like any failed download, and show the drawings","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
